# Intentionally empty.
#
# Second Look ships with ZERO required configuration: `npm install && npm start` must
# work with nothing set. This file exists to document that, not to configure anything.
#
# Everything below is OPTIONAL and has a working default. Set a variable only to
# override that default.
#
# HOST              Interface to bind.            default 127.0.0.1
# PORT              Port to bind.                 default 8787
# SL_CLIENT_DIR     Built client to serve.         default dist/client
# SL_LOG_FILE       Append-only JSONL log path.    default .data/events.jsonl
# SL_LOG_MODE       demo | persist.               default demo (truncate + re-seed on boot)
# SL_ALLOWED_HOSTS  Extra trusted Host values, comma-separated.
# SL_ALLOWED_ORIGINS Extra trusted Origin values, comma-separated.
# SL_MCP_JSON_RESPONSE Set to "1" to answer MCP with application/json instead
# of text/event-stream (useful for minimal third-party clients).
#
# There are no secrets, no API keys and no credentials in this project. The demo
# personas (demo-priya | demo-tom | demo-elena) are non-secret fixture values,
# deliberately labelled, and are documented as such rather than hidden here.
#
# We do not publish OAuth authorization-server metadata, because advertising
# authentication we do not enforce would mislead clients. See the README.